---
import LegalPage from "../components/legal/legal-page.astro";

const toc = [
  { id: "agreement", title: "Agreement to Terms" },
  { id: "registration-tickets", title: "Registration & Tickets" },
  { id: "code-of-conduct", title: "Code of Conduct" },
  { id: "livestreaming-recording", title: "Livestreaming & Recording" },
  { id: "photography-media", title: "Photography & Media Use" },
  { id: "liability-warranty", title: "Liability & Warranty" },
  { id: "privacy-data", title: "Privacy & Data Usage" },
  { id: "changes-cancellations", title: "Changes & Cancellations" },
  { id: "force-majeure", title: "Force Majeure" },
  { id: "intellectual-property", title: "Intellectual Property" },
  { id: "dispute-resolution", title: "Dispute Resolution" },
  { id: "amendments", title: "Amendments" },
  { id: "contact", title: "Contact Information" },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of Service"
  subtitle="The terms and conditions governing participation, ticketing, media use, and rights for IDSW 2026 organized by PERKODI."
  toc={toc}
  currentPath="/terms-of-service">
  <div class="rounded-xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/60 p-5 text-sm text-blue-950">
    <p class="font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-1">Important Notice</p>
    <p class="text-blue-900/90 leading-relaxed">
      By registering for, purchasing a ticket to, or attending <strong
        >Indonesia Software Developer Weekend (IDSW 2026)</strong
      >, whether in-person or virtually, you enter into a legally binding agreement with <strong>PERKODI</strong> and agree
      to comply with these Terms of Service.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 1: Agreement -->
  <section id="agreement" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      1. Agreement to Terms
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      These Terms of Service (“Terms”) constitute a legally binding agreement between you (“Participant”, “Attendee”,
      “Speaker”, “Sponsor”, or “You”) and <strong>Perkumpulan Pengrajin Kode Indonesia (PERKODI)</strong> (“PERKODI”, “We”,
      “Us”, or “Our”), the organizer of <strong>Indonesia Software Developer Weekend 2026 (IDSW 2026)</strong>.
    </p>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      These Terms apply to all participants attending in-person sessions at Usmar Ismail Hall, Jakarta, as well as
      participants joining virtual sessions, workshops, networking channels, and related conference activities. If you
      do not agree with any part of these Terms, please do not register for or attend the event.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: Registration & Tickets -->
  <section id="registration-tickets" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      2. Registration & Tickets
    </h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        <strong>Mandatory Registration:</strong> Valid registration through our official ticketing platform (TipTip) or official
        complimentary pass distribution is required for admission.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sales Policy:</strong> All ticket sales are final and non-refundable, except as explicitly provided in these
        Terms or under exceptional circumstances approved at the sole discretion of the organizers.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>CFP Speaker Refund Exception:</strong> Attendees who purchased a ticket and are subsequently accepted as conference
        speakers are eligible for a full refund upon written request prior to the event.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Non-Transferability:</strong> Tickets are non-transferable unless prior written request is submitted to and
        approved by the organizing committee at least 7 business days before the event.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Right of Refusal:</strong> PERKODI reserves the right to deny or revoke entry to any individual who violates
        safety policies, commits fraud, or fails to adhere to the event Code of Conduct.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3: Code of Conduct -->
  <section id="code-of-conduct" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      3. Code of Conduct
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      All participants, including in-person and online attendees, speakers, sponsors, exhibitors, and staff, must
      strictly abide by the event’s <a href="/code-of-conduct" class="text-primary font-semibold underline"
        >Code of Conduct</a
      >:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        <strong>Respect others:</strong> Discrimination or harassment of any form based on gender, race, religion, disability,
        or physical appearance is strictly prohibited.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Follow all instructions:</strong> Comply immediately with instructions given by IDSW event staff, venue management,
        and security personnel.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Priority:</strong> The safety and comfort of all participants take precedence over all other event activities.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 bg-neutral-100 rounded-lg p-3">
      Violations of the Code of Conduct may result in immediate expulsion from the conference without refund and
      potential referral to relevant authorities.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4: Livestreaming & Recording -->
  <section id="livestreaming-recording" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      4. Livestreaming & Recording
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      By attending IDSW 2026, participants acknowledge and consent to image, audio, and video recordings of sessions and
      auditorium proceedings:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        Recordings may be used for live streaming, official digital archives, educational distribution, or future
        promotional purposes on official IDSW and PERKODI channels.
      </li>
      <li>
        If a participant prefers not to be recorded or included in public video streams, they must notify the organizers
        in writing at least 7 days in advance via <a
          href="mailto:idsw.ticketing@perkodi.org"
          class="text-primary underline">idsw.ticketing@perkodi.org</a
        > so reasonable accommodations (such as designated non-filmed seating zones) can be arranged where feasible.
      </li>
      <li>
        Unauthorized continuous recording, live broadcasting, or commercial redistribution of conference sessions by
        attendees without prior written permission is prohibited.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 5: Photography & Media Use -->
  <section id="photography-media" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      5. Photography & Media Use
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      Official photographers and media crew will capture photos and video footage throughout the conference:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        Event photos or videos featuring attendees may be used for marketing, press releases, social media, recap
        publications, and historical archival purposes.
      </li>
      <li>
        Participants are deemed to consent to the reasonable use of their likeness and image in crowd or candid event
        photography unless they opt out in writing beforehand.
      </li>
      <li>
        To opt out, please contact the organizers prior to the event with a clear self-photograph so our media team can
        make reasonable efforts to exclude your likeness from published highlights.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 6: Liability & Warranty -->
  <section id="liability-warranty" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      6. Liability & Warranty
    </h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        <strong>“As Is” Disclaimer:</strong> All conference activities, presentations, content, sessions, and networking opportunities
        are provided “as is,” without warranties of any kind, express or implied.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Limitation of Liability:</strong> Organizers (PERKODI, community co-hosts, sponsors, and partners) are not
        liable for any personal injury, loss, damage, or theft of personal property occurring during the event or at the venue.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Personal Belongings:</strong> Attendees bear sole responsibility for the custody and safety of their personal
        belongings (laptops, phones, bags, equipment) at all times within Usmar Ismail Hall.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Technical / Content Accuracy:</strong> The views expressed by speakers, sponsors, or attendees belong solely
        to them and do not necessarily reflect the official stance of PERKODI.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 7: Privacy & Data Usage -->
  <section id="privacy-data" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      7. Privacy & Data Usage
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      We treat participant privacy with the utmost seriousness:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        Personal data collected (including full names, email addresses, contact info, job titles, and speaker bios) will
        be used exclusively for event administration, ticketing, credential verification, and essential communication.
      </li>
      <li>
        All personal data handling must comply with Indonesian data protection regulations (Law No. 27/2022 on Personal
        Data Protection / UU PDP).
      </li>
      <li>
        Participant data may be shared with trusted third parties (such as ticketing providers, venue access control,
        and livestreaming platforms) solely where strictly necessary for event execution. We do not sell participant
        data.
      </li>
      <li>
        For comprehensive details on your statutory rights and our data practices, please consult our full <a
          href="/privacy-policy"
          class="text-primary font-semibold underline">Privacy Policy</a
        >.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 8: Changes & Cancellations -->
  <section id="changes-cancellations" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      8. Changes & Cancellations
    </h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        <strong>Program Alterations:</strong> Organizers may change the event format, schedule, speaker lineup, or presentation
        topics at their discretion (e.g., due to speaker travel disruptions or unforeseen circumstances).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Notification:</strong> In case of substantial rescheduling, format changes, or full cancellation, attendees
        and speakers will be informed promptly via the email address supplied at registration and through official website
        announcements.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Remedies:</strong> In the event of partial or full event cancellation by the organizers, attendees will be
        offered reasonable alternatives (e.g., access to virtual proceedings, rescheduling to future dates, or ticket refunds
        where applicable).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>External Costs:</strong> PERKODI and its partners are not liable for any third-party expenses incurred by
        participants, including non-refundable flight, transit, or accommodation bookings.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 9: Force Majeure -->
  <section id="force-majeure" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      9. Force Majeure
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      The organizers are not liable for failure to hold, deliver, or complete the event due to unforeseen events or
      circumstances beyond reasonable control.
    </p>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      Such circumstances include, but are not limited to: natural disasters, severe earthquakes, floods, acts of war,
      civil unrest, strikes, terrorism, widespread utility or power failures, government orders, public health
      emergencies, epidemics, or national lockdowns. In such events, alternative plans, digital arrangements, or refunds
      may be offered at the organizers’ discretion.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 10: Intellectual Property -->
  <section id="intellectual-property" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      10. Intellectual Property
    </h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        <strong>Speaker Ownership:</strong> Speakers retain full intellectual property ownership of their submitted content,
        presentation slides, source code, and workshop materials.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Attendee License:</strong> Attendees are granted non-exclusive, non-commercial rights to access and use shared
        conference materials solely for private study, learning, and research purposes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Organizer Publication Rights:</strong> By presenting at IDSW, speakers grant PERKODI a non-exclusive license
        to record, publish, stream, and archive their presentation materials post-conference for community access.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Trademarks & Branding:</strong> “IDSW”, “Indonesia Software Developer Weekend”, and related conference logos
        are trademarks of PERKODI. Use of these marks for commercial purposes without written authorization is prohibited.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 11: Dispute Resolution -->
  <section id="dispute-resolution" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      11. Dispute Resolution & Governing Law
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      These Terms and any dispute or claim arising out of or in connection with them or your participation in IDSW 2026
      shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the <strong>laws of the Republic of Indonesia</strong>.
    </p>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      The parties agree to attempt in good faith to resolve any dispute amicably through informal negotiations. If a
      dispute cannot be resolved informally, any legal proceeding or action will be tried exclusively in the <strong
        >courts of Jakarta (Pengadilan Negeri di wilayah Jakarta)</strong
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 12: Amendments -->
  <section id="amendments" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      12. Amendments
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      Organizers reserve the right to amend or update these Terms at any time to reflect operational, logistical, or
      legal changes.
    </p>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      Updates will be published immediately on the official IDSW website (<a
        href="https://idsw.dev"
        class="text-primary underline">idsw.dev</a
      >). In the event of material modifications affecting attendee rights, registered participants will be notified via
      email. Continued attendance or participation after such changes constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 13: Contact Information -->
  <section id="contact" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      13. Contact Information
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      For questions, requests for ticket transfers, media opt-out notices, or clarifications regarding these Terms of
      Service, please contact:
    </p>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 p-5 text-sm text-neutral-700">
      <p class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">PERKUMPULAN PENGRAJIN KODE INDONESIA (PERKODI)</p>
      <p class="mt-1">Organizing Committee — IDSW 2026</p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Email: <a href="mailto:idsw.ticketing@perkodi.org" class="text-primary font-semibold underline"
          >idsw.ticketing@perkodi.org</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
